# This repo's own commands. There is no `agentrc` binary, so no check: and no
# probe: — these are scripts you run by path, and their --help is the truth.
#
# The short aliases (cc, cx, …) are NOT here. They live in the shell view,
# where a live `alias` probe reads them back — so they cannot go stale.
name:  agentrc
what:  this repo's own commands — routing, and the setup script
docs:  the README, and each script's own --help

= WHERE ARE MY REQUESTS GOING
omniroute-where  | base URL, both combos, and whether the gateway answers
                 | Run it first whenever an agent behaves oddly
howto            | this reference. `howto --list` for the tools it knows

= CHANGING WHICH MODELS YOU GET
omniroute/switch-combo.sh --to NAME | move the claude combo on every surface
                 | at once: the config file, VS Code's settings, codex's toml
  --codex --to NAME | move the codex combo instead
  --dry-run      | print what would change and touch nothing. Do this first
  --from OLD     | only needed when the current value cannot be read

= THE GATEWAY'S OWN ROUTING TABLE
omniroute/apply-routing.sh --show | every combo, alias and pattern rule it has
  --seed         | write your live gateway state into the config file
  --dry-run      | diff the config against the gateway, change nothing
  (no flag)      | apply the diff
  --prune        | apply, and delete rows the config does not mention
  --probe ID     | after applying, send one 4-token request and report what
                 | actually served it. The only real proof of a route

= SETTING UP A MACHINE
./install.sh --dry-run | what it would link and write
./install.sh     | do it. Safe to run twice
~/.config/based/omniroute | the URL, the key and the combo names. Mode 600,
                 | never in a repo. Everything else is derived from it

= WHY AN ALIAS CAN RETURN THE WRONG MODEL
--dry-run warnings | "no member serves family X" means an alias points at a
                 | combo serving a different family. That returns HTTP 200
                 | with a model you did not ask for, not an error
--probe ID       | settles it. Read the served model, not the status code
